{"ASK_HOMETOWN","reg=civilian,family,worker,rescue|st=friendly,neutral",{"Born and raised in Muldraugh, never left, never wanted to, never will, I guess, now","I grew up in Rosewood, small town, everybody knew my business, I'd give a lot to be known","West Point, my whole family's from West Point, all the way back to the Civil War","Riverside, I swam in that river every summer, it's a different river now","March Ridge, up on the ridge, a hundred people, a church, a gas station, that's it...","Louisville, originally, big city kid, but I came down here for the quiet, and look at me now","Brandenburg, my daddy ran a farm there, I didn't want it, now I'd take it","Irvington, a little town, a big heart, I miss it so much it hurts","Ekron, you've probably never heard of it, a stoplight and a grain elevator, my whole childhood","Valley Station, working-class, hard-working, tough, that's me, tough","Not from here, I came from out of state, Ohio, a visit, a visit that turned into this...","I grew up on a farm outside Fallas Lake, and moved to town for work, now town's the dangerous part","Born in the next county, married a local, stayed, regretted nothing, until this week","Everywhere, I moved around, my father was a trucker, home was the cab","Right here, born and raised","Down by the river, a little place most folks drive through without stopping","I grew up two counties over","Louisville","West Point","Farm country, out past the county line","I'm not from here","I moved around a lot as a kid","I was born in the back bedroom of a farmhouse","Small town, small people, small dreams"},false,false,{[15]={{t="I know every crack in every sidewalk",afterMs=3500}},[16]={{t="I miss it already",afterMs=3200}},[17]={{t="moved here for love",afterMs=3500},{t="stayed for stubbornness",afterMs=3000}},[18]={{t="big city, lots of noise",afterMs=3200},{t="I came down here for quiet",afterMs=2800}},[19]={{t="we have a church, a diner, and a gas station",afterMs=3500},{t="and, once, a very exciting county fair",afterMs=3000}},[20]={{t="you could stand on the porch and see forever",afterMs=3200}},[21]={{t="I was passing through",afterMs=3500},{t="and then everything stopped",afterMs=3000}},[22]={{t="my dad was a trucker",afterMs=3200},{t="home was wherever the truck parked",afterMs=2800}},[23]={{t="my mother says I came out hollering",afterMs=3500}},[24]={{t="and now I'd give anything to go back",afterMs=3200}}}},
